# Review: APPROVED

## Acceptance Criteria Checklist
- [x] Orchestrator uses canonical execution log roles (`planner`, `implementer`, `qa`, `reviewer`, `prompt-reviewer`), with prompt review using `loop_number=None` (`src/workflow/orchestrator.rs:258`, `src/workflow/orchestrator.rs:386`, `src/workflow/orchestrator.rs:530`, `src/workflow/orchestrator.rs:894`, `src/workflow/orchestrator.rs:1086`).
- [x] Log paths are derived via `log_path_for_role(project_dir, loop_number, role)` through `LogWriter::open`, with no log filename derivation from `loop_slug` or backend name (`src/output_log.rs:8`, `src/output_log.rs:77`).
- [x] Log files are opened in append-only mode (`create(true)` + `append(true)`) and never truncated (`src/output_log.rs:97`).
- [x] Each attempt writes a stable separator with attempt number, sanitized backend label, fallback flag, and timestamp (`src/output_log.rs:46`, `src/output_log.rs:106`).
- [x] Timeout/parse-retry/reformatter attempts append to the same `(loop_number, role)` log file via shared `LogWriter` threading through retry paths (`src/workflow/orchestrator.rs:2671`, `src/workflow/orchestrator.rs:2783`).
- [x] Logging is best-effort: open/write/flush failures emit `tracing::warn!`, disable further writes for that run, and do not alter execution result semantics (`src/output_log.rs:81`, `src/output_log.rs:119`).
- [x] Unit tests cover separator formatting, retry-path attempt numbering semantics, and log-writer failure resilience (`src/output_log.rs:228`, `src/output_log.rs:326`, `src/output_log.rs:361`, `src/output_log.rs:413`, `src/output_log.rs:303`).
- [x] Conformance tests `retry_append_behavior` and `prompt_reviewer_path` were added and registered (`src/validate/tests_streaming.rs:13`, `src/validate/tests_streaming.rs:17`, `src/validate/mod.rs:23`, `src/validate/mod.rs:91`).
- [x] Verification evidence: `cargo test -q` passed; `./target/debug/ralph validate --bin ./target/debug/ralph --filter streaming` passed both new streaming tests.

## Notes
Implementation aligns with the Loop 2 feature spec for append-only retry attribution logging. The previously requested retry-path conformance and attempt-numbering test gaps are now addressed.

